From: ADB Stability Fix
Date: Thu, 2 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix ADB disconnect issue by reducing XHCI interrupt moderation interval

The ColorOS11 branch has an aggressive interrupt moderation interval (160us)
which causes data buffering to overflow during high-bandwidth ADB operations
like logcat. This patch reduces the interval to 40us to process interrupts
more frequently, matching the stability of oppo-oss branch.

Root cause: When the ER_IRQ_INTERVAL is set to 160, the xHCI host controller
delays interrupt processing by ~5ms. During continuous ADB logcat streaming,
USB gadget TX/RX buffers overflow, causing the connection to drop and recover.

Solution: Lower the interval to 40us (~1.25ms delay) to prevent buffer overflow
while maintaining reasonable CPU efficiency.

---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c
@@ -678,7 +678,7 @@ int xhci_run(struct usb_hcd *hcd)
 	xhci_dbg_trace(xhci, trace_xhci_dbg_init,
 			"// Set the interrupt moderation register");
 	temp = readl(&xhci->ir_set->irq_control);
 	temp &= ~ER_IRQ_INTERVAL_MASK;
 	/*
 	 * the increment interval is 8 times as much as that defined
 	 * in xHCI spec on MTK's controller
 	 */
-	temp |= (u32) ((xhci->quirks & XHCI_MTK_HOST) ? 20 : 160);
+	temp |= (u32) ((xhci->quirks & XHCI_MTK_HOST) ? 20 : 40);
 	writel(temp, &xhci->ir_set->irq_control);
 
 	/* Set the HCD state before we enable the irqs */

